        // wrap_placement facet: an extract/map lambda body sits in a
        // MapperS-EXPECTING position — the map*-method lambda must return a MapperS
        // (mapSingleToItem's shape is Function<MapperS<T>, MapperS<F>>). Two SINGLE
        // body forms that compile to a non-MapperS are converted to match golden —
        // a bare-FUNCTION-call body (UNWRAPPED by renderImplicitFunctionInvocation,
        // right for the boolean filter-predicate position) wraps in MapperS.of, and
        // an existence check `exists(...)` (a ComparisonResult — a Mapper<Boolean>,
        // but NOT a MapperS) appends .asMapper(). Gated to a SINGLE body
        // (mapSingleToItem / mapItem): a MULTI body wraps in MapperC.of, a
        // co-blocked cardinality sibling handled by MAPPER_C_EXPECTING (facet
        // bareInvocationMapperCWrap, PR #278): a MULTI body wraps a bare FUNCTION
        // invocation in MapperC.of (rule-scoped); a non-bare MULTI body is emitted
        // exactly as compiled (identical to the prior NEUTRAL routing). See
        // {@link #compileLambda(RInlineFunction, ExpressionContext,
        // ExpressionCompiler, LambdaBodyPosition)}.
        // facet multiCondBaseThenArg (PR #350, F2b): the bound-MapperC scoped conditional
        // descent (see mapMethod) also lifts the lambda position — the mapItemToList
        // ladder body renders through the MAPPER_C_EXPECTING admit.
        // facet thenBindingOverlay (v3.1 C2d retirement family 9, PR #616) — VERDICT-MOVED
        // RETIRE-AFTER-CENSUS -> JUSTIFIED-KEPT (the seat-30 bar; S08): the triage's proposed
        // channel OVER-FIRES at 16,895 arrivals. c9 census, 83,097 arrivals (28,327 / 28,327 /
        // 26,443): `compute(argument) == MULTI OR chainProvesMulti(argument)` agrees at
        // 66,190/83,097 (79.65%) with T/T 2,262, T/F 12, F/T 16,895 over THIRTEEN signatures. Both
        // directions are fatal and neither disjunct is safe alone — the largest signature (4,898)
        // is cardCompute=SINGLE with chainProvesMulti=true, the second (3,616) the converse, so
        // their OR is worse than either. The 12 T/F are exactly the class the note above describes
        // (a MULTI conditional base reading SINGLE off the rule path, carrier
        // fn:GetUnderlierProductIdentifierLeg1), now measured at 12. astLoL was logged as a third
        // candidate and is true at only 171 of 83,097.
        JavaType posBoundT = boundImplicitReceiverType(expr, ctx.scope());
        var posTu = compiler.getTypeUtil();
        boolean posBoundMapperC = posBoundT != null && posTu != null
                && posTu.isMapperC(posBoundT);
        // facet lolDefaultBodyMulti (v3.1 flip seat 33, law A.4, rung 2): the
        // list-PRESERVING map method's lambda sits in a MapperC-EXPECTING position. The
        // runtime signatures are the whole argument: MapperListOfLists.mapListToList takes a
        // `Function<MapperC<T>, MapperC<F>>` (rune-runtime MapperListOfLists:94) where
        // mapListToItem takes `Function<MapperC<T>, MapperS<F>>`, so the position must follow
