            // isOutputListOfLists + isBodyMulti branch — MapperListOfLists to
            // MapperListOfLists); the SINGLE body keeps the list-consuming
            // mapListToItem. Green-safe by construction: mapListToItem's lambda
            // returns MapperS, so a MULTI (MapperC-valued) body under the old
            // unconditional arm never compiled — no green file carries it.
            // facet lolDefaultBodyMulti (v3.1 flip seat 33, law A.4, rung 1): a `default`
            // body whose left or right operand is the BARE PIPED ITEM is MULTI under a bound
            // list-of-lists receiver, so the step keeps the list. GOLDEN <- FORK: golden
            // GetBasketConstituents x drr 7.0-7.3 renders
            // `.mapListToList(item -> MapperC.of(Collections.singletonList(...)))` where the
            // fork consumed the list with `.mapListToItem(item -> MapperS.of(...))`. Under a
            // BOUND MapperListOfLists receiver the implicit `item` IS the inner list - golden's
            // own `item.getMulti()` on the very same line is the proof - so the joined body is
            // multi. Neither AST computer can see it: CardinalityComputer answers SINGLE for
            // every RDefaultExpr, and the #363 arm inside isBodyMulti consults
            // chainProvesMulti BOTH-STRICT, whose left operand here is a SINGLE-output function
            // call. The read therefore lives HERE, at the ONE seat where `boundT` has already
            // proved the receiver kind (render truth), and NOT in the parser's computer -
            // CardinalityComputer:189 is DO-NOT-TOUCH.
            //
            // MEASURED (LAW 75, [P32-LOLBODY], route-identical): the complete bound-LoL
            // population is 60 rows / 6 `where=`, and the ONLY `bodyKind=RDefaultExpr` rows in
            // it are the carrier's 8; the implicit-operand conjunct is strictly narrower still.
            // Corpus-dead by census: `mapListToList(` occurs in 4 of the 174,141 goldens
            // (GetBasketConstituents x drr 7.0-7.3) and 0 fork files on BOTH routes.
            //
            // TWO CONSEQUENCES COME FREE through the ONE `mapMethodKind` SOT (the #274
            // two-halves-agree law): the thenArg DECL, because producesListOfLists already
            // admits `MapMethod.LIST_TO_LIST`; and the NEXT step's
            // `mapListToItem`, because its receiver now binds to a MapperListOfLists.
            // LAW 74: javac33 PRE 526/527 -> 0.
            boolean lolDefaultMulti = expr.body() != null
                    && expr.body().body()
                            instanceof com.regnosys.rosetta.ast.expressions.binary.RDefaultExpr lolDef
                    && (lolDef.rawLeft()
                                instanceof com.regnosys.rosetta.ast.expressions.references.RImplicitVariable
                            || lolDef.rawRight()
                                instanceof com.regnosys.rosetta.ast.expressions.references.RImplicitVariable);
