            // ONLY_ELEMENT-rooted level — facet collapseGetSuffix, v3.1 C2d retirement family 7,
            // PR #614: that arm's own gate moved off the rendered `.get()` tail onto
            // HandlerHelper.bareOnlyElementCollapse, and the decline is now STRUCTURAL rather than
            // textual, because THIS arm fires only for `k == 0 && base instanceof RSymbolReference`
            // — a bare rule reference is never an RListOpExpr), so this assignment is not
            // load-bearing for them — it is stated explicitly rather than relied on implicitly.
            if (ruleWrapValue != null) {
                declValueStr = ruleWrapValue;
            }
            // facet thenChainFnValueWrapOnce (seat 20, PR #592), rung E: the arm CONSULTS the
            // render's wrap-factory truth (`valExpr.unwrapToBuilder().isEmpty()` — the very guard
            // the #339 arm below has always carried, LAW 69). The "#308 raw List" contract this
            // arm was written against is no longer what the render does for every explicit multi
            // call: ReferenceHandler.tryMultiValueWrap (facet multi_cardinality_value_wrap) hands
            // back the `MapperC.<T>of(fn.evaluate(…))` WRAP FACTORY when the callee's multi output
            // resolves, and the arm then wrapped it AGAIN — `MapperC.<ReportingRegime>of(MapperC
            // .<ReportingRegime>of(extractRegimeInformation.evaluate(…)))`, drr 6.36–6.38
            // NatureOfCounterparty2Rule/NatureOfTheCounterparty2Rule + drr 7.x GetUnderlyingAssetName,
            // DTCC_UnderlyingAssetReportRule, UnderlyingIdOtherDTCCRule, UnderlyingIdOtherSourceDTCCRule
            // (22 sites, the seat-20 probe; the form compiles — MapperC implements MapperBuilder,
            // so it is a parity heal, not a compile repair). Where tryMultiValueWrap declines (a
