            // probed sites) the value is still the raw `fn.evaluate(…)` and the arm wraps exactly
            // as before. Byte-neutral for every non-factory value by construction; the rings are
            // the receipt. Green-safe: ZERO of the 179,209 goldens carry the single-argument
            // double wrap (the seat-20 static census).
            boolean wrappedByMultiFnArm = false;
            if (!single && !listOfLists
                    && argExpr instanceof RSymbolReference fnValRef
                    && fnValRef.symbol().filter(RFunction.class::isInstance)
                            .map(RFunction.class::cast)
                            .flatMap(RFunction::output)
                            .map(out -> gm.isMulti(out)).orElse(false)
                    && valExpr.unwrapToBuilder().isEmpty()) {
                declValueStr = "MapperC.<" + elementName + ">of(" + declValueStr + ")";
                wrappedByMultiFnArm = true;
            }
            // facet deepBareInvokableThenHoist (PR #339): a bare-invokable level compiles to
            // the receiver `.evaluate(…)` form, which is BARE for a bare-FUNCTION
            // (renderImplicitFunctionInvocation emits `fn.evaluate(…)`, no wrap) and
            // pre-wrapped `MapperS.of(rule.evaluate(…))` for a bare-RULE
            // (renderImplicitRuleInvocation always wraps) — the #276 dual wrap-factory law.
            // Wrap the bare form so the decl compiles (`final MapperS<Party> thenArg0 =
            // MapperS.of(extract_BrokerId.evaluate(item.get()));` — golden BrokerId), keyed on
            // the AST being a bare-invokable at this level (k==0: the chain BASE is a bare
            // no-arg call; k>0: the preceding then's body is) AND the compiled value not
            // already being a wrap-factory (unwrapToBuilder — belt-and-suspenders, the
            // isInvocationWrapFactory pattern; the #333 MapperC.<T>of multi-fn-base arm above
            // already wrapped its own case). The single MapperS wrap carries no witness
            // (golden emits none); a multi bare body mirrors the #333 MapperC.<T>of form.
            // facet thenChainFnValueWrapOnce (seat 20): the predicate and the two wrap forms now
            // live in the shared helpers (bareInvokableValueNeedsWrap / wrapBareInvokableValue),
            // consulted here, at the filter receiver and at FunctionExpressionRenderer's
            // single-then decl — byte-neutral at this seat by construction (the identical
            // predicate: a bare no-arg RRule/RFunction reference whose value is not a wrap factory;
            // the identical forms), the rings the receipt.
            if (!listOfLists && !wrappedByMultiFnArm) {
                RExpression bareLevelExpr = (k == 0) ? base
                        : thens.get(k - 1).body().map(f -> f.body()).orElse(null);
                if (bareInvokableValueNeedsWrap(bareLevelExpr, valExpr)) {
                    declValueStr = wrapBareInvokableValue(declValueStr, single, elementName);
                }
            }
            // An INTERMEDIATE bare-item only-element level (`then only-element` mid-chain)
            // compiles to the raw `<prev>.get()` collapse — a BARE item that does not
            // compile against the Mapper decl. Wrap it MapperS.of(...) like the consumer
            // arm below (golden TotalNotionalQuantityOfLeg1's `final MapperS<BigDecimal>
            // thenArg3 = MapperS.of(thenArg2.get());`) — the #260 thenArgMapperSWrap law
            // at the deep seat, with the SAME rendered-shape guard the SET-seat arm uses
            // (the collapse can compile selfUnwrapping — unwrapToBuilder present — so it
            // sits OUTSIDE the wrap-factory-gated block above).
            // facet distinctOnlyElementRewrap (PR #359, F-1): the `then distinct
            // only-element` sibling — the collapse renders `distinct(thenArgN).get()`
            // (the #168-armA prefix-distinct + the single-coercion `.get()`), a BARE
            // item against the MapperS decl exactly like the bare-item form; golden
            // re-wraps `MapperS.of(distinct(thenArg0).get())` (the ExecutionAgent
            // family ×12, drr Rules). Same rendered-shape guards; DISTINCT over the
            // bare item only (evidence-capped — a nav-argument distinct stays
            // declined, missed-flip-at-worst).
            // facet navOnlyElementDeclRewrap (PR #371, F-A1): the #260/#359 collapse
            // re-wrap widened to (a) the k==0 BASE level (declLevelExpr already folds
            // base vs previous-then-body) and (b) a NAV-rooted ONLY_ELEMENT collapse
            // (`payout -> optionPayout only-element` as a then-chain base inside a
            // conditional arm — the LoadTypeRule esma/fca/DTCC trio: golden
            // `final MapperS<OptionPayout> _thenArg2 = MapperS.of(item.<Payout>map(…)
            // .<OptionPayout>mapC(…).get());`). The #359 evidence-cap on bare-item-only
            // is lifted BY the trio's nav carriers; the rendered-shape guards (a bare
            // `.get()` collapse, not already wrap-factored) still arbitrate — a bare
            // item against the MapperS decl never compiled, so green files cannot
            // carry the unwrapped form (the #339 green-safe-by-construction argument).
            // facet collapseGetSuffix (v3.1 C2d retirement family 7, PR #614): the rendered-shape
            // arbiter the four comments above call "the SAME rendered-shape guard" is now the
            // TYPED one — HandlerHelper.bareOnlyElementCollapse (an ONLY_ELEMENT root over a
            // null-typed compiled value). The c7b census at this seat: 3,188 arrivals, text=true
            // at 684, and `typeNull AND one-of-the-four-shapes AND ONLY_ELEMENT` selects exactly
            // that set on all three walks (default D11, IR D11, optimised) with no counterexample.
            // The four shape predicates below each already require ONLY_ELEMENT at the root, so
