            // over all 4,062 corpus .rosetta files finds `then … extract … (switch` at
            // exactly FOUR sites, all four that same basket rule in drr 7.0-7.3, and
            // 7.0.0's is the SET-seat green twin this arm never sees. The 41-file
            // `extract (switch` superset is the #353 BASE-position population
            // (MapReturnSwap*/MapEquitySwap*, the mas rule), untouched by a BODY arm. The
            // one corpus NEAR-MISS is the iosco cde v1 price rule's FirstExerciseDate
            // (`then extract trade [ … extract [ style switch … ] ]`): its body ROOT is a
            // nested extract, not the switch, so the ROOT test declines it.
            //
            // Green-safe by the standing runtime-`.then(` corpus law as well: the runtime
            // carries no Mapper.then(Function) at all, so ZERO of the 34,686 goldens carry
